# AES-256-GCM encryption key for GithubToken.tokenEncrypted (Module 6 —
# see docs/stages/06-submission-verification.md Section 5 and
# docs/DECISIONS.md D96). Read by both the api container (encrypts a
# token on admin entry) and the worker container (decrypts it right
# before calling the GitHub API) — the two must be mounted with the
# exact same value.
#
# Copy this file to github_token_key.txt (gitignored) and fill in a
# real random value. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Rotating this value makes every previously-stored GithubToken
# undecryptable — re-add them after rotating.
change-me-to-a-long-random-value
